.TH DENIAL-PORTAL 1 "August 2026" "Denial" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
denial-portal \- serve Denial's desktop Settings portal backend
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B denial-portal
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B denial-portal
is the D-Bus-activated backend for
.BR org.freedesktop.impl.portal.Settings .
It publishes Denial's committed
.B org.freedesktop.appearance/color-scheme
preference and resolved
.B org.freedesktop.appearance/accent-color
to the XDG desktop portal frontend.
.PP
The process connects to
.BR deniald (1)
over a private same-user Unix seqpacket socket and receives a complete,
revisioned appearance snapshot before claiming its D-Bus name. It does not
read or write Denial's settings file. Stale snapshots are ignored and
.B SettingChanged
is emitted only when the public portal value changes.
.PP
This program is an internal session component. It is normally started by user
D-Bus activation or
.BR denial-portal.service ;
interactive invocation is not required.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/denial/portal.sock
Mode-0600 private state channel owned by the compositor.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/denial/accent-color-v1
Last resolved accent, atomically maintained by the portal IPC worker.
.TP
.I /usr/share/xdg-desktop-portal/portals/denial.portal
Portal backend descriptor.
.TP
.I /usr/share/dbus-1/services/org.freedesktop.impl.portal.desktop.denial.service
User D-Bus activation metadata.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/denial-portal.service
Optional systemd user unit, bound to Denial's graphical-session target.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates that the compositor ended the private connection normally.
Connection, protocol, or D-Bus failures return nonzero.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR deniald (1),
.BR denial-session (1),
.BR xdg-desktop-portal (1)
